+++ b/README.md
@@ -1,33 +1,40 @@
-# LogIn-Advanced API
+# LogIn-Advanced
 
-This repository now contains an ASP.NET Core Web API (`Api` project) alongside the original WPF application.
-The API exposes the same user management logic through OpenAPI (Swagger) so endpoints can be tested via tools such as Postman.
+This repository contains an ASP.NET Core Web API (`Api` project) and a Blazor WebAssembly frontend
+(`BlazorFrontend` project). Shared models are located in `BlazorFrontend.Shared`.
+The API exposes the user management logic through OpenAPI (Swagger) so endpoints can be tested via tools such as Postman, while
+the Blazor client consumes the same endpoints for a web-based UI.
 
-## Building the API
+## Building
 
 ```bash
-# build only the API project
-dotnet build Api/Api.csproj -c Release
+# build all projects
+dotnet build test.sln -c Release
 ```
 
 ## Running
 
 ```bash
 # run the API
 cd Api
 dotnet run
+
+# in another terminal run the Blazor client
+cd ../BlazorFrontend
+dotnet run
 ```
 
-When running in development the API serves Swagger UI at `http://localhost:5000/swagger`.
+When running in development the API serves Swagger UI at `http://localhost:5287/swagger` and the Blazor app is available at
+`http://localhost:5002` by default.
 
 ## Available Endpoints
 
 - `POST /login` – verify username and password.
 - `GET /users` – list all users.
 - `GET /users/{username}` – get a specific user.
 - `POST /users` – create a new user.
 - `PUT /users/{id}` – update an existing user.
 - `DELETE /users/{username}` – delete a user.
 - `PUT /users/{id}/description` – update only the description field.
 
 The same models and data access logic from the WPF application were kept so behavior matches the UI version.
